.TH FL-GREET 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-greet \- graphical greeter for greetd
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-greet\fR [\fB\-\-demo\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A login screen for greetd(1). Run it inside the cage kiosk compositor, e.g. in
\fI/etc/greetd/config.toml\fR: command = "cage \-s \-d \-\- fl-greet".
Sessions are read from /usr/share/wayland-sessions. \fI/etc/fldesktop/greeter.ini\fR
[Greeter] accepts Background, MinUid and HideUsers (comma separated).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-demo\fR
Run without greetd; any user logs in with the password "demo".
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-session\fR(1), \fBfl-panel\fR(1)
